/ `toPose` when the box moved), `tallFridge.zone.select`, `tallFridge.zone.drag` (`index`, `from`, `to` heights). Rule breaks from a tall saved before the split (a door under the fridge, a drawer above it, two side panels) are yellow `fridgeRuleIssues` lines, never removed. `cabinet.migrate` (`from`, `to`) = an old `generalTallCabinet` with a fridge zone opened as `tallFridgeCabinet`.
- **Neighbour yield** (`renderer/yield.js`; today only the fridge cabinet triggers it): an edit that makes a cabinet grow into another one is not refused. `yield.prompt` (`id` the grown cabinet, `why` the edit kind, `grow` world direction, `neighbours` `[{id, face {axis, dir} local, label, by (mm of overlap), ok, reason}]`) — the neighbours turn red (`job.getConflict()`, not saved) and the panel asks. `yield.apply` (`changed`, `done` `[{id, face, by, from, to {envelope, pose}}]`, `left` the ones that could not) = "Yes": each neighbour's facing face is pushed back by `by` through its own `resizeFace` (zones follow that module's Resize rules), far face stays, one undo step. `yield.decline` = "No": the checks keep the red line and an Auto-fix button. `reason` examples: `its left side is fixed` (not in `resizeFaces`), `W would be N, under its minimum M`, `a zone would go under its minimum`, a generator error. Cabinet-to-cabinet overlap is now a red check (`cab-a overlaps cabinet cab-b`) in the space checks and blocks export; modules with `attach` (bed box, bed side table) are not counted against the body.
- **Base is two modules** (rail Base → Ensuite / Kitchen, same kitchen generator). **Kitchen** = `kitchenCabinet`: today's base, including a stove zone; a job saved before the split stays this id. **Ensuite** = `ensuiteCabinet`: the same carcass and the same zones except stove. A stove on an ensuite is a red `generator.errors` line `Ensuite has no stove — zone … in column …`; the zone is not rewritten as a door. Both boxes include the door in D. A partition fit (`wall.fit.kitchenId`) accepts either as the base. `kitchen.cell.*` is the editor for both. Style 1 cuts a LED T-groove on the underside of B3 unless `ledGroove` is false (`kitchen.cell.led`); style 2 does not. `kitchen.cell.kick` (`from`, `to`) is the typed kick height (BCH) on the kitchen page; zones re-fit to cabinet height minus that. `kitchen.cell.sink` (`on`) on a left or right door drops the upper hinge 130 mm; a bench sink will set that later. `kitchen.wheel` (`on` true|false) is the **Wheel arch avoidance** checkbox at the top of the Kitchen and Ensuite page. On, with a floor-plan pair, rewrites `wheelAvoidances` from that pair; on, with no pair, adds, edits, or removes a hand arch (`x0`, `x1`, `height`, `depth`). Off clears the cut. `kitchen.size` (`key` `W`|`D`|`H`, `from`, `to`, `face` `left`|`right` for width, `back` for depth, `bottom` for height, `changed`) is a typed outer size on the kitchen page. Width asks which face moves, then which column takes the change when there is more than one (`column` is that column's index). `kitchen.waterfall` (`from`, `to` `left`|`right`|null, `column`, `length`) turns the drop on or off; the outer width stays and that column gives or gains the 25 mm. A first width drag in 3D asks the same question and remembers the column for the next drag. Depth keeps the back and moves the front. Height keeps the bottom and grows upward. The same fields are on the other box modules (`ohc.size`, `uohc.size`, `tall.size`, `tallFridge.size`, `small.size`, `lounge.size`, `bedside.size`, `cabinet.size`). Overhead and U overhead keep the ceiling (`face: "top"`). A fridge width stays on the cut-out. Bedroom, bunk and bed box sizes that come from the space or the body stay read-only. `kitchen.split` (`on`, `after` the column index to the left of the joint, `x`, `from` when removed) turns Split Kitchen on or off. `kitchen.split.move` (`from`, `to`, `x`, `changed`, `where: "front view"`) drags the arrow; it only sits on a line between columns, never on an outer end. A run longer than 2400 mm warns until both sides are at most that. A wheel arch is cut only on the carcass whose width it overlaps. An ensuite bottom side-door zone can set `applianceFloorEnabled` (`kitchen.cell.washer`): a deck behind B3 plus two kick supports. It is refused on a kitchen, on style 2, under 450 mm carcass depth, under 500 mm clear width, or when the column meets a wheel arch.
