n the left (`heir`), or the one on the right when the first column is removed) / `kitchen.cell.blocked` (`reason`). A kick-height change re-fits every column's zones to height − kick. Zones inside a column are stored **top-down** (zones[0] is the highest, z1 = H), and a column width drag keeps the order and total length. Resolved cell rectangles come from `result.debug.columns` (generator-resolved `x0/x1`, `z0/z1` — never recomputed in the panel). The generator can emit a valid cabinet **with** `validation.errors` (e.g. the documented V1 half-slot conflict) — the front view still renders; a "blank front view" report is boards/columns missing, not an error entry.
