struction: "classic"` = `golden-i`): the L main run on its own — `i_front` full length covering `i_left_end` / `i_right_end`, `back_rail`, `i_left/right_support`, `i_rail_back/front`. A run whose lid area passes `FRAME_LID_MAX_LENGTH` 1600 (I, or the L main run) gets equal lids `<run>_lid_1..k`, 2 apart, each gap over a `<run>_mid_support_j` that halves over both rails — a "lid split in the wrong place / too many lids" report is that rule, not a param. **PARALLEL is a frame too** (default; `classic` = `golden-parallel`; 19'6 Rear Door = `rear-door-parallel`): each run is built like the L wing — `<side>_side` (seat front toward the gap, cut round the wheel-arch cover), `<side>_front` (aisle end), `<side>_outer_support` (on the end wall) / `<side>_inner_support` (on the seat front), `<side>_lid` on them, and `<side>_rear_rail` which **always lies on the wall** (y = D − c − T..D − c), from the end wall into a **half slot** (groove `for: <side>_rear_rail`, depth T/2, never through) on the seat front's inner face, down to the cover top `avoidanceHeight` when the wheel arch is on. A "rail shows from the gap / rail on the wrong wall" report is this layout. `aisleAccess: "DRAWER"` (panel "Aisle ends" → Drawer, `lounge.run.access`) puts the L wing drawer (`<side>_drawer_strip` / `_front` / `_rail`) at both aisle ends. The middle cabinet is on by default when the gap takes 300 (`hasMiddleCabinet` unset), its width the gap when narrower than 600; it has only width / depth / height — it stands on the wheel-arch cover's top when there is one, else on the floor (`startHeight` is ignored on the frame parallel); `result.params.middleCabinet` is what was built (null = none); `lounge.run.midCab` carries `key: "middleCabinet.width"` etc. for the panel's size fields; `generator.errors` `Middle cabinet width N exceeds the middle gap G` = it would stand in the seats. `generator.errors` `Parallel: the wheel-arch depth / height …` = the cover would cut the rail or the aisle end. The middle