l"`, `seat` `{width, snap, locked, moved}`, `params` totalWidth / depth / height / singleLoungeWidth, `pose`; `how` click | enter — Enter without moving takes min(560, length / 2)). Esc = `lounge.back` to the box. Wheel arch and middle cabinet are then set in the panel (the cabinet is on by default when the gap takes 300). **Lounge I in 3D** (rail Lounge → I): the same box placement, three clicks (`place.anchor` / `place.face` / `place.corner` with feature snaps and inference, `moduleId: loungeGenerator`), then straight `lounge.finish` (`style: "I"`, `anchor`, `corner`, `locked`, `plane`, `extrude`, `clamped`, `box`, `front` = the room face as for L, `params` mainWidth = length along that face / mainDepth / height, `pose`). Before 2026-09-29 the I used a floor-only flow (`lounge.point` / `lounge.face`, grid snap only — no feature points); a "first point does not snap" report in an old log is that. The floor-plan Lounge tool still uses the older corner / face / side / width flow (`lounge.place.*`).
